  "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of logarithms, we observe that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+5x+4{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061((1+x)(1+4x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x),$ we recall the standard result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x) & =x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo obtain the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+4x),$ we replace $x$ with $4x$ in the standard expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+4x) & =(4x)-\\frac{1}{2}(4x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(4x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(4x)^{4}+\u22ef \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{1}{2}(16{x}^{2})+\\frac{1}{3}(64{x}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(256{x}^{4})+\u22ef \\\\  & =4x-8{x}^{2}+\\frac{64{x}^{3}}{3}-64{x}^{4}+\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the two series to give the desired result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+5x+4{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+4x) \\\\  & =(x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\u22ef)+(4x-8{x}^{2}+\\frac{64{x}^{3}}{3}-\u22ef) \\\\  & =(1+4)x+(-\\frac{1}{2}-8){x}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{64}{3}){x}^{3}+\u22ef \\\\  & =5x-\\frac{17{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{65}{3}{x}^{3}+\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$",
